| The Help domain screen pads each name with `for (j = strlen(NAME); j != N; j++)`: the god-table pad stops at 10 and the Contents pad at 12. A longer name never reaches N, so the int16 `j` wraps and appends about 65,000 underscores, which fill the 8192-line help buffer and cut off the rest of the screen. Plain loop logic with no platform or typedef dependence, so Win32 fails the same way for a god name over 10 characters. Both pads now stop with `j < N`; the god table adds one separator for a name of 10 or more (`src/Help.cpp`). The Contents pad has no live trigger (longest domain name is 11). | **Observed** -- `tools/check_help_truncation.sh`: before, the domain case is RED (final entry missing; The Multitude is 13 characters); after, all four cases are GREEN. | Not sent | inc-pu6v.341 |
| `Thing::Remove` reads `m->Fields` again after each `EV_FIELDOFF` throw, but a field event can take the Thing off the map (seed 22: Rainstorm's leave-effect kills a creature through `Magic::Blast`, `Creature::Damage` and `Creature::Death`, which calls `Remove`; the nested `Remove` already threw `EV_FIELDOFF` for every field at the square and cleared `m`), so the outer loop reads through NULL. Plain control flow, no platform, typedef or compiler dependence (`src/Display.cpp`). | **Observed** -- `tools/check_remove_field_event.sh`: the handler scene never returns before the fix (harness exit 139, check exit 1) and returns with three events delivered after (exit 0); `dive-short.keys` seed 22 exited 139 before and 0 after. | Not sent | inc-5lval |
| `FirstInv()`/`NextInv()` kept the walk cursor in one function-local static per class (`Character::GetInv`, `Monster::GetInv`), so a walk begun inside another walk of the same class moved the outer cursor: an inner walk that ran to the end stopped the outer walk early, and one that broke left the cursor mid-pack so the outer walk revisited items and could loop forever. Plain shared state with no platform or typedef dependence, so Win32 fails the same way. Each cursor is now one file-scope struct, and a scoped `InvCursorGuard` saves both on entry to `CalcValues`, `SkillKitMod`, `HasSkillKit`, `LucubrationPickable`, `RealThrow` and `VMachine::Execute` and restores them on every exit; a restored cursor whose item was destroyed or left the walking creature's pack ends the walk (`src/Inv.cpp`, `inc/Creature.h`). | **Observed** -- `tools/check_inv_cursor.sh` (`bane-radius.keys`, seed 1, `xsummon-priest-seed5-opt0822.char`, `tools/fixtures/options-2026-08-22.dat`, `INCURSION_INV_CURSOR_PROBE=1`): before, an outer walk of 33 items visited 1 (early stop) and a nested break ran to 133 visits (stopped at 4x); after, 33 of 33 in the unnested order, and a walk whose next item is destroyed or dropped to the floor never returns it. | Not sent | inc-y2fkq |
| `Effect "Detonate"` walks a monster-targeted creature's inventory for the first mundane item with `while (hTarget->isMagic())` and no NULL stop, so a victim carrying no items or only magic items leaves `hTarget` NULL and the next read crashes the script. Plain script logic with no platform or typedef dependence, so Win32 crashes the same way. Now stops at `NULL_OBJ` and returns ABORT with nothing detonated (`lib/alchemy.irh`). | **Observed** -- `tools/check_detonate_null_target.sh`: unfixed null scene FAIL (exit 139, "Detonate NULL object reference"), control scene PASS; fixed both PASS. | Not sent | inc-3nvr4 |
| `Character::Exchange` returned with the global `isExchange` still true on a cursed-weapon refusal and on death mid-swap, so every later `Wield` skipped its two-handed prompt. Plain control flow with no platform or typedef dependence, so Win32 misbehaves the same. Now every exit path resets it (`src/Inv.cpp`). | **Traced** -- every `return` in `Exchange` read; no run reproduces it. | Not sent | inc-h5aql |
| Sheathing a weapon provokes an attack of opportunity under SRD 3.5 and drawing one does not, yet no wield, take-off or `Character::Exchange` path called `ProvokeAoO`. Plain game logic, so Win32 misbehaves the same. Now `Character::ChangeToSet` and `Character::TakeOff` provoke once when a held weapon is put away (`src/Inv.cpp`). | **Observed** -- `tools/check_weapon_sets.sh` AC8 counted 0 goblin attacks of opportunity before and 1 after for `-`, and 0 with the call removed against 1 with it for the forced switch; the take-off path is Traced (no `ProvokeAoO` call before) and counts 1 after. | Not sent | inc-h5aql |
| The generated `VMachine::GetMemberVar` read a thing's map as `oThing(h)->m->myHandle` with no null test, so a script read of `X->m` on a thing off the map (removed, in a pack, not yet placed) dereferenced NULL. The generator emits the same read on every platform and compiler, so Win32 upstream faults identically (`src/RComp.cpp`, `GenerateDispatch`; output `lib/dispatch.h`). | **Observed** on the pantheon branch under lldb; **Traced** on master (no script reaches it) -- `tools/check_script_map_read.sh`, seed 3, options-2026-08-22, `INCURSION_MAPREAD_PROBE`: unguarded exits 139, guarded returns 0. | not sent | inc-m2c6 |
| In the script language `break;` left only a `switch` (no loop pushed a break target, so `break;` in a loop did nothing and in a loop inside a switch left the switch), and `continue;` was resolved only by `for` (a bare `while` or `do` ignored it, and a `while` inside a `for` jumped to the `for`'s increment). Plain compiler logic with no platform or typedef dependence, so the original Win32 compiler emits the same code (`lang/Grammar.acc`, `src/yygram.cpp`, `src/RComp.cpp`). | **Observed** -- `tools/check_script_loops.sh`, `tools/keys/inc-b0ii-join.keys`, `tools/fixtures/options-2026-08-22.dat`: before, a `while`, `for` and `do` loop with `break;` at its third pass ran ten passes (`n=10`) and `continue;` in a bare `while` skipped nothing (`n=10`); after, `n=3` and `n=5`. Three shipped scripts change behavior: `lib/prestige.irh` Loremaster book search, `lib/wspells.irh` NPC rope choice, `lib/pspells.irh` Command spell Attack (audit in bd inc-b0ii). `VBlock::ProcessContinues` also moved too few bytes when it inserted the extended jump word for a `continue;` more than 511 words before the loop body's end: it passed an entry count to `memmove` as a byte count, so the loop code after the insert was cut off (`src/RComp.cpp`). Case `n` of the same check: with the old count the run printed no result line; with the byte count `n=800 g=800 m=5`. | No | inc-b0ii |
| `SetPVal` (`src/VMachine.cpp`) wrote the power value in place through `e.EMagic`, which every cast site points at the module's SHARED effect resource, so one cast permanently changed the spell's power for every later reader and a loaded game (module data is not in a save) read the original value and diverged from the live one. The in-place write is in the first commit (7b8504a3) and misbehaves identically on Win32. SetPVal now copies the component into the event (`EventInfo::EMagicCopy`, declared in inc/Events.h) and writes the copy; `Magic::CalcEffect` and `TEffect::Power` read the power value through `e.EMagic` after the script (in src/Magic.cpp). | **Observed** -- `tools/check_pval_shared.sh`, `tools/keys/pval-shared-cast.keys`, `tools/fixtures/options-2026-08-22.dat`, fixture `human-priest-mage-seed4-gate`: before, after one Mage Armour cast the shared pval read `0d0+6` (the written value); after, it stays `15d1-107` (the module's level-scaled value) and the cast still grants magnitude 6 (`vDmg=6`; the SetPVal change alone made it 15). Nine illusion spells in `lib/wspells.irh` ran SetPVal in `PRE(EV_MAGIC_HIT)`, after `e.vDmg` was fixed, so they only worked through the leak; the call moved to `EV_CALC_EFFECT`. `tools/check_illusion_cr.sh`: Phantasmal Force creature CR 0 before the move, 2 (= Illusion skill 4 / 2) after. | No | inc-q4kjl |
| `Creature::Walk` dereferenced `m` after `ThrowXY(EV_PUSH, ...)` returned: the push walk can remove the mover through `Creature::TerrainEffects`, leaving `m` NULL, and the next lines (`m->FCreatureAt`) crash. Plain control flow, no platform or typedef dependence, so Win32 crashes the same way. Now returns DONE when the mover is dead or off the map, as the `ProvokeAoO` branch below it already did (`src/Move.cpp`). | **Observed** -- `tools/headless.sh tools/keys/dive-depth-4.keys 16` with `tools/gates/Options.Dat`: SIGSEGV (exit 139) in `Creature::Walk` before, exit 0 after; a UBSan build named the null-`Map` call at `src/Move.cpp` (the silent-move loop). Found when the inc-qapjo random-stream shift reached it; the stack at the removal was Walk, ThrowXY, Walk, TerrainEffects, Thing::Remove. | No | inc-qapjo |
| A monster must never displace a friendly creature or the player: `Creature::Walk` let any monster swap squares with a friendly blocker, so two friendly horses following the player swapped places forever. Now only the player displaces a friendly creature, and the strength-shove branch is skipped for friendlies. Pure game logic with no platform or typedef dependence, so the original Win32 build swaps identically (`src/Move.cpp`). | **Observed** -- `tools/check_knf4d_friendly_displace.sh`, `INCURSION_DISPLACE_PROBE`: before, AC1, AC3, AC4/horse and AC4/player FAIL (monster mover swaps with a friendly horse and with the player); after, all five pass, with AC5 (player displacement) green throughout. | Not sent | inc-knf4d |
| `Trap::TriggerTrap` wrote the trap's data into its caller's event (isTrap, vCasterLev, eID, EItem, EVictim), and its `ReThrow` copied the finished run back, leaving efNum one past the trap's last part and EMagic NULL. Dispel Magic (`lib/wspells.irh`) calls it for a non-mundane trap that resists the dispel and restores only eID, so the next globe square ran with that state and Ice Floor's `EV_MAGIC_XY` (`lib/dungeon.irh`) faulted on `e.aval`. Now the trap runs on its own copy of the event on `EventStack`, as `RedirectEff` does (`src/Feature.cpp`). Upstream has the same `TriggerTrap` and the same Dispel Magic handler, so Win32 with the original typedefs and compiler crashes the same way. | **Observed** -- `tools/check_dispel_trap_event.sh` (probe `INCURSION_DISPEL_TRAP_PROBE`): fixed PASS, fix reverted exit 139; seed 8 of `tools/keys/dive-short.keys` with `tools/gates/Options.Dat` exits 139 with the fix reverted and 0 with it. | Not sent | inc-gxsnp |
